WEBVTT

00:00:02.160 --> 00:02:40.810
Key, hide and seek really isn't my game.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:03:01.210
Oliver, this isn't funny.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.210
Where are you?

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:17.319
Cops will have a key.

00:03:17.319 --> 00:04:47.389
I know I have a big appetite, but you get enough food here to feed a small army.

00:04:47.389 --> 00:04:51.389
Well, I thought it would be a good idea to invite a few people over for Thanksgiving this year.

00:04:51.389 --> 00:04:55.389
Actually, I was hoping we could keep it low-key.

00:04:55.389 --> 00:04:57.389
I'm not feeling very thankful this year.

00:04:57.389 --> 00:05:01.389
Well, I know it's going to be a hard day, Clark, especially after what just happened to Ryan.

00:05:01.389 --> 00:05:04.389
But company could help.

00:05:04.389 --> 00:05:06.389
It was dad's holiday. He carved a turkey.

00:05:06.389 --> 00:05:07.389
Carved the turkey.

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:10.250
Carved this year.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:16.300
He was the one who made sure we all said what we were thankful for.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:20.300
I always made sure that I was thankful for my abilities.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.300
But you know what, he was wrong.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:26.800
If I was normal, he would still be here.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.800
Carving the turkey with Grandpa's old carving knife.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:35.660
Hey.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:39.660
So you can scratch Oliver's name off the Thanksgiving guest list,

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.660
or any other guest lists, for that matter.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:47.439
Too bad, what happened?

00:05:47.439 --> 00:05:50.420
Last night he pulled another one of his trademark, disappearing

00:05:50.439 --> 00:05:51.439
acts.

00:05:51.439 --> 00:05:53.439
Smack in the middle of a date.

00:05:53.439 --> 00:05:54.439
No.

00:05:54.439 --> 00:05:55.439
I'm sorry, Lois.

00:05:55.439 --> 00:05:58.439
Oh, don't be. I mean, who's kidding who here?

00:05:58.439 --> 00:06:00.439
We had no future.

00:06:00.439 --> 00:06:05.439
He's a world-known billionaire, and, uh, I am a nail-biting, talent-douling, tabloid reporter.

00:06:05.439 --> 00:06:08.439
Lois, I'm sure you'll find someone who's better suited for you.

00:06:08.439 --> 00:06:09.439
Yeah.

00:06:09.439 --> 00:06:11.439
I know, I know. Life goes on.

00:06:11.439 --> 00:06:14.439
At least for some people.

00:06:14.439 --> 00:06:16.439
Have you heard the news?

00:06:16.439 --> 00:06:19.439
The Green Arrow was shot last night.

00:06:19.439 --> 00:06:20.439
It said, you know.

00:06:20.439 --> 00:06:24.180
today's planet.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:26.180
A man found him bleeding and ran for help,

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:27.680
but when the cops finally got there,

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.680
all that was left was a bloodstain.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:46.569
Found the charitable organization I want to focus on.

00:06:46.569 --> 00:06:49.569
It's Second Chance Halfway House.

00:06:49.569 --> 00:06:52.569
I have the time, and I heard you mention their name on the phone,

00:06:52.569 --> 00:06:55.569
and then I found this brochure.

00:06:55.569 --> 00:06:57.569
What an amazing program.

00:06:57.569 --> 00:06:59.569
I don't see why they can't be in every city in this country.

00:06:59.569 --> 00:07:03.569
Lana, you'd be in contact with the violent criminals

00:07:03.569 --> 00:07:05.569
just released from prison.

00:07:05.569 --> 00:07:06.569
Maybe.

00:07:06.569 --> 00:07:10.569
from time to time, but mostly I beat the central office.

00:07:10.569 --> 00:07:13.569
Why not channel your energy into the Youth Foundation

00:07:13.569 --> 00:07:15.569
or the Center for Victims' Rights?

00:07:15.569 --> 00:07:17.569
Because this is what I want to do.

00:07:17.569 --> 00:07:19.569
I'm just trying to protect you.

00:07:19.569 --> 00:07:25.360
What is it with people feeling like they have to protect me?

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:28.360
Lex, I don't need to be watched over.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.360
I didn't say you did.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:32.360
I want you to be safe.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:34.360
Well, this isn't about what you want.

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:37.360
This is about what I want.

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:40.360
Pick any other project.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.360
I'm sorry.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:08:09.990
You're looking off for healthy.

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:13.879
It's called exercise, Clark.

00:08:13.879 --> 00:08:16.879
It's something we mere mortals have to do from time to time.

00:08:16.879 --> 00:08:20.879
According to the Daily Planet, the Green Arrow was shot last night.

00:08:20.879 --> 00:08:23.879
If I was shot, don't you think I'd be laying in a hospital or a morgue?

00:08:23.879 --> 00:08:26.879
I'm not bulletproof like you are, Clark.

00:08:26.879 --> 00:08:31.879
Besides, you of all people should know better than to believe everything you read in the newspaper.

00:08:31.879 --> 00:08:33.879
It's the Daily Planet, not the Inquisitor.

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:34.879
A witness saw you look.

00:08:34.879 --> 00:08:36.879
lying in a pool of blood.

00:08:36.879 --> 00:08:46.220
Well, maybe it was someone else with a preference for green.

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:48.220
What's your green arrow gear doing out in the middle of the room?

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:56.850
I'm uploading video. Check this out.

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:58.850
See that?

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:03.850
Now I've got footage of the scumb bags, so if they try to get away, I can track them down.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:05.850
Oliver, you're getting sloppy.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.850
Your gear's out in the middle of the room. The door's unlocked.

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:09.850
That could have been lowest coming through the door.

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:12.850
Yeah, you know what? I've had a lot of my mind lately, all right?

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:15.850
Apparently you were too busy using your powers of Bail Hayden to realize that there's a crime wave in Metropolis.

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:19.129
a crime wave in Metropolis.

00:09:19.129 --> 00:09:21.129
Let me ask you a question.

00:09:21.129 --> 00:09:24.129
Are you ever going to get off your ass and finally do something for a change?

00:09:24.129 --> 00:09:26.129
You can come here to be insulted.

00:09:26.129 --> 00:09:28.129
Well, you know what? There's the door, Clark. I don't remember you being invited.

00:09:28.129 --> 00:09:30.129
Oliver, what's going on with you?

00:09:30.129 --> 00:09:34.129
Clark, I don't need to take advice from someone who's only worry in life

00:09:34.129 --> 00:09:36.129
is to protect his own identity.

00:09:36.129 --> 00:09:37.129
That's a lie. You know it.

00:09:37.129 --> 00:09:38.129
Let me tell you something.

00:09:38.129 --> 00:09:40.129
When I'm out there, when I'm out on the streets, I'm protecting people.

00:09:40.129 --> 00:09:44.129
All right, I got much bigger things to worry about, like staying alive.

00:09:44.129 --> 00:09:55.409
You okay?

00:09:56.409 --> 00:09:57.409
Fine, just get out of here.

00:09:57.409 --> 00:09:58.409
You sure?

00:09:58.409 --> 00:10:53.549
Go!

00:10:53.549 --> 00:10:55.549
Since when did you turn the apartment into a florist shop?

00:10:55.549 --> 00:10:57.549
They're from Oliver.

00:10:57.549 --> 00:10:58.549
Wait a second.

00:10:58.549 --> 00:11:02.549
The guy smothers you with flowers and you forget everything he's done?

00:11:02.549 --> 00:11:04.549
Please, I'm not that gullible.

00:11:04.549 --> 00:11:08.549
The whole botanical overkill is just a lame attempt to beg forgiveness.

00:11:08.549 --> 00:11:12.549
Well, if he shows up in person to beg for forgiveness, don't answer the door.

00:11:12.549 --> 00:11:16.549
Lois, I went to talk to him at his apartment.

00:11:16.549 --> 00:11:18.549
You didn't.

00:11:18.549 --> 00:11:19.549
What were you thinking?

00:11:19.549 --> 00:11:20.549
I was looking out for him.

00:11:20.549 --> 00:11:21.549
for you.

00:11:21.549 --> 00:11:22.549
I have 20-20 vision in Smallville.

00:11:22.549 --> 00:11:23.549
I look out for myself.

00:11:23.549 --> 00:11:27.549
When I was in his apartment, I found a needle in his syringe.

00:11:27.549 --> 00:11:31.549
Unless your doctor prescribed, I think Oliver's doing drugs.

00:11:31.549 --> 00:11:34.549
This actually explains a lot.

00:11:34.549 --> 00:11:36.549
All those times he disappeared.

00:11:36.549 --> 00:11:40.570
I should have known.

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:43.570
He said that Thanksgiving was a hard time a year.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:45.570
Made him think about his parents.

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:47.570
Lois, I think you might want to keep your distance.

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:52.620
He is a substance abuse problem, not leprosy.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:53.620
And I am not going to abandon him.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:55.620
I'm not going to abandon him when he needs me the most.

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.620
He's not himself right now.

00:11:57.620 --> 00:12:00.620
And based on his behavior, I don't think he's someone you want to be around.

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:03.620
Well, see, that's the difference between you and me, Clark.

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:05.620
I don't deserve people when they need help.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:14.850
You're a miracle worker, Doc.

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:16.850
We need to talk, Mr. Queen.

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:17.850
We certainly do.

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:21.850
I finally found myself injured badly enough to use the RL 65.

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:23.850
And it works.

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:24.850
Perfectly.

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:25.850
And not just once.

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:31.159
I cut my hand, and after one injection, I was completely healed.

00:12:31.159 --> 00:12:32.159
Well, don't take any more.

00:12:32.159 --> 00:12:36.159
The last time I checked, doctor, you work for me.

00:12:36.159 --> 00:12:39.159
The lab mice have been exhibiting irrational cognitive behavior

00:12:39.159 --> 00:12:41.159
and more troubling, violent tendencies.

00:12:41.159 --> 00:12:43.159
I'm not a mouse, I'd feel fine.

00:12:43.159 --> 00:12:46.159
Do you? No lapses in judgment?

00:12:46.159 --> 00:12:48.159
No sudden outburst of anger?

00:12:48.159 --> 00:12:53.570
Not really, but I am starting to feel one coming on right now.

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:56.570
It's not worth risking possible psychosis just so you can climb out Everest

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:58.570
or parachute out of your Learjet.

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:01.570
This isn't about my recreational activities, doctor.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:02.570
We're on the verge of a member.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:05.570
We're on the verge of a medical breakthrough that could save countless lives.

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:09.820
I'm more than honored to be the guinea pig.

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:19.889
Trust me, I can handle the occasional temper tantrum.

00:13:19.889 --> 00:13:30.139
I'll talk to you after the break, Senator.

00:13:30.139 --> 00:13:34.539
You have a happy Thanksgiving, too.

00:13:34.539 --> 00:13:35.539
Bye-bye.

00:13:35.539 --> 00:13:42.529
Hi!

00:13:42.529 --> 00:13:45.529
Come on in. I was just about to call you.

00:13:45.529 --> 00:13:47.529
I didn't get your RASEP.

00:13:47.529 --> 00:13:50.529
Ah, well, that is why I'm here.

00:13:50.529 --> 00:13:58.929
I, uh, came in person to, uh, tell you that I, uh, won't be coming for, uh...

00:13:58.929 --> 00:14:01.980
Well, that's too.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:04.980
Too bad. I was really looking forward to seeing you.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:12.320
After Lillian died, I somehow decided that I would stop celebrating Thanksgiving.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:16.320
Why don't you make an exception and celebrate with us? We'd really love to have you.

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:21.179
And I don't think Clark would agree.

00:14:21.179 --> 00:14:27.179
The holiday is going to be difficult this year without extra complications for.

00:14:27.179 --> 00:14:35.870
You're not a complication, Lionel. You're a part of my life now, and I'm very thankful for that.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:41.710
I'm very thankful for that.

00:14:41.710 --> 00:15:06.049
Do you know what that means to me?

00:15:06.049 --> 00:15:23.080
I'd mean to.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:25.080
I take it this wasn't a party favor.

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:26.080
I broke into his apartment.

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:28.080
There might be some residue still left on.

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:30.080
I'll call Oliver Queen a lot of things,

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:32.080
but I never thought I'd call him a junkie.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:34.080
Boy, I don't think he's getting high.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:38.080
Come on, Clark. You of all people should know that everyone has the secrets.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.080
Besides, it's not that much of a stretch to think that a jet-setting billionaire

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.080
might have a little habit to hide.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:45.080
Well, can you just get it checked out? We'll know for sure.

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.080
Yeah.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:48.080
I'll text my biochem buddy. It meant you.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:50.080
Hopefully he hasn't left for Thanksgiving already.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:53.080
Hey, that Green Arrow story, did that victim actually see him get shot?

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:54.080
No.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:59.080
But the people that own the car did come forward and say that he saved him from a carjacking that night.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:01.080
He hasn't been spotted since.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:06.080
Um, so I'm just going to get this syringe to my chemist.

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:10.080
Great. Why don't you head out and I will get a hold of you as soon as I find anything?

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:11.080
Try to get rid of me?

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:14.080
No. Why would I want to do that?

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:27.669
Us girls were just going to get some lunch.

00:16:27.669 --> 00:16:28.669
It's great. Uh,

00:16:28.669 --> 00:16:30.669
Have a good time.

00:16:30.669 --> 00:16:37.179
That wasn't awkward at all.

00:16:37.179 --> 00:16:41.179
I tried to keep the heavenly bodies from colliding, but there's only so much I can do.

00:16:41.179 --> 00:16:43.179
I want you to check something out for me before you go.

00:16:43.179 --> 00:16:46.179
Yeah. Okay. My Google is your Google. What do you need?

00:16:46.179 --> 00:16:50.179
I'm curious about this halfway house that Luther Corp Foundation supports.

00:16:50.179 --> 00:16:53.179
I offered to get involved, but Lex won't let me anywhere near it. He says it isn't safe.

00:16:53.179 --> 00:16:57.179
Well, most halfway houses aren't exactly in these mid-farks, Lana.

00:16:57.179 --> 00:16:59.179
I don't think that's it.

00:16:59.179 --> 00:17:02.179
Lex swears that he's honest with me, but lately he's...

00:17:02.179 --> 00:17:04.180
lately he's been a little secretive.

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:08.980
I don't know, maybe I'm reading into it.

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:11.980
No, I think you're just being cautious, which is smart.

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:13.980
Don't worry. We'll figure things out.

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:27.019
Are you all right?

00:17:27.019 --> 00:17:29.019
From where I was sitting, it looked like you fainted.

00:17:29.019 --> 00:17:31.019
Let's get to the doctor.

00:17:31.019 --> 00:17:33.019
No, it's okay. Can we keep my little siesta between us?

00:17:33.019 --> 00:17:35.019
I really wouldn't want anyone to worry.

00:17:35.019 --> 00:17:39.019
Well, it's a little late for that, but yeah, okay.

00:17:39.019 --> 00:19:30.779
Three times. All in the last month.

00:19:30.779 --> 00:19:35.099
And these headaches you've been having, would you describe the pain as

00:19:35.099 --> 00:19:36.099
sharp or don't?

00:19:36.099 --> 00:19:39.099
A sharp, like a knife.

00:19:39.099 --> 00:19:41.099
And it's getting worse.

00:19:41.099 --> 00:19:45.099
I've tried all of the over-the-counter pain relievers, but none of them work.

00:19:45.099 --> 00:19:50.490
There's just migraids, right?

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:52.490
Just a few more tests. We'll have a clearer picture.

00:19:52.490 --> 00:20:10.009
I'm so glad you came here.

00:20:10.009 --> 00:20:13.009
Haven't been able to stop thinking about...

00:20:13.009 --> 00:20:15.009
About what happened.

00:20:15.009 --> 00:20:17.009
I... I wanted to apologize for...

00:20:17.009 --> 00:20:20.009
I didn't come here for an apology, Lionel.

00:20:20.009 --> 00:20:21.009
You did nothing wrong.

00:20:21.009 --> 00:20:22.009
I did.

00:20:22.009 --> 00:20:23.009
I had no right to presume...

00:20:23.009 --> 00:20:24.009
to presume that I could...

00:20:24.009 --> 00:20:25.009
Oh, no, look.

00:20:25.009 --> 00:20:28.289
There's something between us.

00:20:28.289 --> 00:20:33.750
What it is, I don't think either of us knows,

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:36.750
but I do know I'm not ready to find out.

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:44.700
I don't think you do understand.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:49.240
I value our relationship.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:53.839
I really want you to be with me for Thanksgiving.

00:20:53.839 --> 00:21:08.250
Of course.

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:10.250
Lois, what happened?

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:13.250
Well, lucky for me, I walked in on Green Arrow

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.250
pulling a reverse Santa Claus on Oliver's apartment.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.250
The Green Arrow did this to you?

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:19.250
I guess it was only.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:22.250
Only a matter of time before he hit up the new billionaire in town?

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:26.250
Luckily, I was able to get in a few solid licks of my own.

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:28.250
He'll be nursing a couple broken ribs for sure.

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:30.250
Have you talked to Oliver yet?

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:33.589
Has he visited you here in the hospital?

00:21:33.589 --> 00:21:34.589
No.

00:21:34.589 --> 00:21:41.309
I tried him on all his numbers, and he was nowhere to be found.

00:21:41.309 --> 00:21:43.309
Clark, I'm nervous.

00:21:43.309 --> 00:21:45.309
Either he's on some kind of crazy drug bender

00:21:45.309 --> 00:21:47.309
or a green arrow has gotten to.

00:21:47.309 --> 00:21:48.309
Loz, don't worry.

00:21:48.309 --> 00:21:51.309
Promise I'll do everything I can to track him down.

00:21:51.309 --> 00:21:52.309
Yeah.

00:21:52.309 --> 00:21:53.309
That'll be a big help.

00:21:53.309 --> 00:21:55.309
Look, I'll just call Chloe.

00:21:55.309 --> 00:22:11.200
I'll take that.

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:12.200
I put a bullet in your chest.

00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:14.200
Now you're gonna pay for it.

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:18.930
I don't think so.

00:22:18.930 --> 00:22:44.380
Now let go me.

00:22:44.380 --> 00:22:46.380
You tell me how you were able to heal her.

00:22:46.380 --> 00:22:47.380
I'm calling the cops.

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:48.380
You call the cops anyway.

00:22:48.380 --> 00:22:49.380
You may be able to heal it.

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:51.380
That doesn't mean you don't feel afraid.

00:22:51.380 --> 00:22:54.380
Let go!

00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:56.380
You start talking!

00:22:56.380 --> 00:22:57.380
There's this doctor.

00:22:57.380 --> 00:22:58.380
Comes to the halfway house.

00:22:58.380 --> 00:23:01.380
We get these shots. They say are vitamins.

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:02.380
That's some kind of vitamin.

00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:03.380
Huh?

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:04.380
What's the doctor's name?

00:23:04.380 --> 00:23:06.380
How am I supposed to know?

00:23:06.380 --> 00:23:07.380
What does he look like?

00:23:07.380 --> 00:23:09.380
It's not he.

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:11.380
She's a chick.

00:23:11.380 --> 00:23:26.890
Waste not, want not.

00:23:26.890 --> 00:23:30.890
What happened, Doctor? Bad Batch?

00:23:30.890 --> 00:23:32.890
Project shut down.

00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:35.890
Look, I might have come into this game a little late,

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:38.890
but I'm paying you a lot more than Queen.

00:23:38.890 --> 00:23:40.890
He isn't shutting down anything.

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:42.890
You're right. I am.

00:23:42.890 --> 00:23:44.890
And I could care less about your petty rivalry.

00:23:44.890 --> 00:23:48.890
This is gone beyond one-upmanship, Doctor.

00:23:48.890 --> 00:23:51.890
Your research is now a personal cause of mine.

00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:54.890
Find another cause. I won't be responsible for any more violence.

00:23:54.890 --> 00:23:57.890
Well, you should have thought about that when you took my money.

00:23:57.890 --> 00:24:00.890
I admit I was blinded by greed.

00:24:00.890 --> 00:24:04.890
But now that people are getting hurt, money means nothing to me.

00:24:04.890 --> 00:24:06.890
I'm going back to the drawing board.

00:24:06.890 --> 00:24:09.890
All existing RL-65 is being destroyed.

00:24:09.890 --> 00:24:13.890
I'm sorry, doctor. I can't let you do that.

00:24:13.890 --> 00:24:14.890
I let you do that.

00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:24.940
How's Lois?

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:25.940
Physically, she's fine.

00:24:25.940 --> 00:24:26.940
She's looking for all of her.

00:24:26.940 --> 00:24:28.940
I can't find him anywhere.

00:24:28.940 --> 00:24:29.940
Maybe this will help.

00:24:29.940 --> 00:24:33.940
My science geek analyzed the liquid in that syringe, and you're right.

00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:35.940
No one's going to take it and go to a rave.

00:24:35.940 --> 00:24:40.940
It's a cutting-edge molecular modifier that has something to do with tissue regeneration.

00:24:40.940 --> 00:24:42.940
So it has some sort of healing power?

00:24:42.940 --> 00:24:43.940
Conceivably.

00:24:43.940 --> 00:24:48.940
But according to my Einstein, it also packs a mean punch to a certain part of your brain called the amygdala,

00:24:48.940 --> 00:24:50.940
which triggers violent and aggressive behavior.

00:24:50.940 --> 00:24:54.940
Now, why in God's name would Oliver be injecting something like that?

00:24:54.940 --> 00:24:55.940
I don't know.

00:24:55.940 --> 00:24:58.940
But we better find him before he does something he regrets.

00:24:58.940 --> 00:25:05.680
Who created the drug?

00:25:05.680 --> 00:25:08.680
A woman named Pamela Black is the only one doing that level of research.

00:25:08.680 --> 00:25:14.680
She's a professor at Princeton and has been taking a recent sabbatical to work with Queen Industries.

00:25:14.680 --> 00:25:16.680
If she's supplying the drugs,

00:25:16.680 --> 00:25:18.680
then most likely Oliver's going to show up for more.

00:25:18.680 --> 00:25:50.450
And her place has been completely pillaged.

00:25:50.450 --> 00:25:53.450
If drugs or no drugs, I can't believe Oliver would kill someone.

00:25:53.450 --> 00:25:54.450
kill someone.

00:25:54.450 --> 00:25:56.450
I don't think it was Oliver, Clark.

00:25:56.450 --> 00:26:00.180
It was a green arrow.

00:26:00.180 --> 00:26:04.180
Looks like our green heroes made the leap from Robin Hood to cold-blooded killer.

00:26:04.180 --> 00:26:08.180
I just understand why a scientist was his target.

00:26:08.180 --> 00:26:18.859
Chloe, these folders are from a halfway house metropolis.

00:26:18.859 --> 00:26:20.859
It's called Second Chance.

00:26:20.859 --> 00:26:24.859
This doctor, she was given the kids the same drugs Oliver was taking.

00:26:24.859 --> 00:26:28.859
Lex's foundation funds this halfway house.

00:26:28.859 --> 00:26:31.859
Lex co-opted Oliver's scientist.

00:26:31.859 --> 00:26:34.859
Those two have been at each other since high school.

00:26:34.859 --> 00:26:36.859
And the Green Arrow got in the way.

00:26:36.859 --> 00:26:38.859
Ever, the crusader for the underprivileged,

00:26:38.859 --> 00:26:43.859
he must have gotten wind of Dr. Black's secret experiments and taking care of her his own way.

00:26:43.859 --> 00:26:47.859
If a Green Arrow found out that Luthorpor is behind this, Lex could be the next target.

00:26:47.859 --> 00:27:18.380
I'm sorry. I'm looking for Lex.

00:27:18.380 --> 00:27:19.380
He's not here.

00:27:19.380 --> 00:27:30.849
You okay? Anna, what is it?

00:27:30.849 --> 00:27:40.279
It's nothing. I'm fine.

00:27:40.279 --> 00:27:47.470
You don't look fine. You can talk to me. It's okay.

00:27:47.470 --> 00:27:56.380
Do you ever wish that you could go back?

00:27:56.380 --> 00:28:00.759
in time and everything would be different.

00:28:00.759 --> 00:28:08.029
All the time.

00:28:08.029 --> 00:28:25.869
What did Lex do?

00:28:25.869 --> 00:28:26.869
You didn't do anything.

00:28:26.869 --> 00:28:31.269
If you're in trouble, Lana, I can help.

00:28:31.269 --> 00:28:33.269
Clerk, this has nothing to do with you.

00:28:33.269 --> 00:28:36.579
Could you please just go?

00:28:36.579 --> 00:29:11.380
The car's ready, sir.

00:29:11.380 --> 00:29:22.660
Sorry, Luther.

00:29:22.660 --> 00:29:26.259
Work's not over yet.

00:29:26.259 --> 00:29:31.299
What if this?

00:29:31.299 --> 00:29:33.299
Sign on the dotted line and all your assets

00:29:33.299 --> 00:29:35.299
would be divided among the 50 global charities listed below.

00:29:35.299 --> 00:29:38.299
Would you mind telling me what I've done to deserve this?

00:29:38.299 --> 00:29:41.299
After your lofty support of the second chance,

00:29:41.299 --> 00:29:43.299
Halfway House, I think it's a natural step.

00:29:43.299 --> 00:29:45.299
I went by to check out the facility.

00:29:45.299 --> 00:29:47.299
After some gentle prodding,

00:29:47.299 --> 00:29:50.299
the director told me what you and Dr. Black were doing to the residence.

00:29:50.299 --> 00:29:51.299
He was lying.

00:29:51.299 --> 00:29:54.299
So then I went to go pay the good doctor a visit, and guess what?

00:29:54.299 --> 00:29:56.299
She's dead.

00:29:56.299 --> 00:30:02.539
I knew you weren't a Saint Luther, but killing a woman to cover your tracks?

00:30:02.539 --> 00:30:04.539
You're delusional.

00:30:04.539 --> 00:30:07.539
Sign it.

00:30:07.539 --> 00:30:20.160
What the hell are you doing?

00:30:20.160 --> 00:30:21.160
It's out of anger.

00:30:21.160 --> 00:30:27.799
Drop it!

00:30:27.799 --> 00:30:28.799
You first.

00:30:28.799 --> 00:30:30.799
What do you think is faster?

00:30:30.799 --> 00:30:35.230
An arrow or a bullet?

00:30:35.230 --> 00:31:12.690
There's only one way to find out.

00:31:12.690 --> 00:31:14.690
He pulled a gun, Clark. I had no choice.

00:31:14.690 --> 00:31:16.690
Lex?

00:31:16.690 --> 00:31:18.690
Lex?

00:31:18.690 --> 00:31:22.579
Now I'll let nature take his course.

00:31:22.579 --> 00:31:24.579
Oliver, that's the drug's talking.

00:31:24.579 --> 00:31:26.579
It's not you.

00:31:26.579 --> 00:31:28.579
Hey, that drug is the best thing that ever happened to me, Clark.

00:31:28.579 --> 00:31:31.579
I'm not bulletproof like you, alright?

00:31:31.579 --> 00:31:34.579
I gotta do whatever it takes. I need that drug.

00:31:34.579 --> 00:31:36.579
Oliver! You're not a killer!

00:31:36.579 --> 00:31:37.579
No, but he is, Clark.

00:31:37.579 --> 00:31:38.579
You listen to me. You aren't.

00:31:38.579 --> 00:31:44.970
and I both know the world's a better place without Lex Luthor.

00:31:44.970 --> 00:31:46.970
It's not for us to decide.

00:31:46.970 --> 00:31:47.970
Oliver.

00:31:47.970 --> 00:31:49.970
We're the drugs.

00:31:49.970 --> 00:32:27.970
Lex, he took it all. He took it all from the lab.

00:32:27.970 --> 00:32:28.970
You killed him.

00:32:28.970 --> 00:32:33.740
He killed him.

00:32:33.740 --> 00:33:46.109
You're dealing with Jekyll or Hyde.

00:33:46.109 --> 00:33:48.109
Plain old Oliver today, Clark.

00:33:48.109 --> 00:33:50.109
You haven't broken any glasses.

00:33:50.109 --> 00:33:52.109
That's a good sign.

00:33:52.109 --> 00:33:54.420
Right.

00:33:54.420 --> 00:33:55.420
What made you come to your senses?

00:33:55.420 --> 00:34:02.099
Actually, you did.

00:34:02.099 --> 00:34:04.099
This whole time, I just wanted to be like Clark Kent.

00:34:04.099 --> 00:34:05.099
You know, I wanted to, uh...

00:34:05.099 --> 00:34:09.079
I wanted to have the ability to bring justice to the world

00:34:09.079 --> 00:34:10.079
without having to work.

00:34:10.079 --> 00:34:12.079
about getting killed in the process.

00:34:12.079 --> 00:34:17.699
And then something occurred to me, you know, I realized that, uh,

00:34:17.699 --> 00:34:18.699
um,

00:34:18.699 --> 00:34:21.699
Clark Kent would never take another man's life.

00:34:21.699 --> 00:34:25.519
I came within an inch of doing just that.

00:34:25.519 --> 00:34:35.329
I'm not even in your league.

00:34:35.329 --> 00:34:39.090
You do a lot of good in this world.

00:34:39.090 --> 00:34:41.090
You don't need to be indestructible to be a hero.

00:34:41.090 --> 00:34:43.090
Yeah.

00:34:43.090 --> 00:34:45.090
No, you're right, you're right. Yeah, um,

00:34:45.090 --> 00:34:47.090
I should be thankful for who I am, right?

00:34:47.090 --> 00:34:49.090
the abilities that I have. I know that.

00:34:49.090 --> 00:34:58.780
Me too. Come on, you can't be alone on Thanksgiving.

00:34:58.780 --> 00:35:00.780
Birds waiting.

00:35:00.780 --> 00:35:01.780
Thanks, Clark.

00:35:01.780 --> 00:35:03.780
I, uh, I appreciate the offer, but I can't.

00:35:03.780 --> 00:35:07.699
Look, Lois is gonna be there,

00:35:07.699 --> 00:35:10.699
and I'm pretty sure she doesn't even want to be in the same zip code as me, so.

00:35:10.699 --> 00:35:12.699
Now that you're back on track,

00:35:12.699 --> 00:35:15.699
I'm sure Lois is gonna want you there.

00:35:15.699 --> 00:35:17.699
Trust me.

00:35:17.699 --> 00:35:19.699
Well, trust you.

00:35:19.699 --> 00:35:21.699
What happened to all the lectures about guys with secret identities

00:35:21.699 --> 00:35:23.699
not being able to handle relationships?

00:35:23.699 --> 00:35:28.739
The truth is, you and I are different.

00:35:28.739 --> 00:35:30.739
And Lois isn't Lana.

00:35:30.739 --> 00:35:35.250
If you two are meant to be together, then who am I to stand in the way?

00:35:35.250 --> 00:35:55.320
Are you feeling any better?

00:35:55.320 --> 00:35:56.320
You better?

00:35:56.320 --> 00:35:57.320
Hanging in there.

00:35:57.320 --> 00:35:59.630
I'll make yourself comfortable.

00:35:59.630 --> 00:36:04.630
I, uh, did my due diligence on the Second Chances Halfway House, and I found...

00:36:04.630 --> 00:36:10.869
Oh, I'm not here to talk about the Halfway House.

00:36:10.869 --> 00:36:12.869
Okay.

00:36:12.869 --> 00:36:14.869
But there's some stuff I think you should know about, Lana.

00:36:14.869 --> 00:36:15.869
About Lex?

00:36:15.869 --> 00:36:18.869
I, uh, don't want to hear anything more about Lex.

00:36:18.869 --> 00:36:19.869
I can't.

00:36:19.869 --> 00:36:24.780
What's going on?

00:36:24.780 --> 00:36:28.260
Lana, what happened?

00:36:28.260 --> 00:36:30.260
Hey, you know you can tell me anything.

00:36:30.260 --> 00:37:10.050
I'm pregnant.

00:37:10.050 --> 00:37:11.050
Did you cook that on the barbecue?

00:37:11.050 --> 00:37:15.050
It's a little crispy on the outside, but it's what's on the inside.

00:37:15.050 --> 00:37:16.050
It counts.

00:37:16.050 --> 00:37:17.050
I'm sure it's delicious.

00:37:17.050 --> 00:37:20.050
Clark, would you put the hot plate on the table, please?

00:37:20.050 --> 00:37:22.050
You talked to Oliver today?

00:37:22.050 --> 00:37:24.050
Don't go there, Smallville.

00:37:24.050 --> 00:37:30.880
I think that's for you.

00:37:30.880 --> 00:37:39.699
Jimmy says hi from his mom's house and ever the reporter.

00:37:39.699 --> 00:37:40.699
He has news.

00:37:40.699 --> 00:37:43.699
I guess the Metropolis PD arrested Pamela Black's killer,

00:37:43.699 --> 00:37:45.699
and you were right.

00:37:45.699 --> 00:37:46.699
It wasn't the Green Arrow.

00:37:46.699 --> 00:37:49.699
It was some kit from the Halfway House.

00:37:49.699 --> 00:37:50.699
I'd bet anything that Lex is somehow behind.

00:37:50.699 --> 00:37:52.699
that Lex is somehow behind this.

00:37:52.699 --> 00:37:53.699
Maybe.

00:37:53.699 --> 00:37:55.699
I doubt we'll be able to prove it, though.

00:37:55.699 --> 00:37:58.699
I guarantee you Lex's shredders are doing some serious overtime.

00:37:58.699 --> 00:38:00.699
Does Lana know about this?

00:38:00.699 --> 00:38:02.699
Well, she said I went by the mansion the other day,

00:38:02.699 --> 00:38:04.699
and she was really upset about something.

00:38:04.699 --> 00:38:05.699
Is she alright?

00:38:05.699 --> 00:38:08.429
Yeah.

00:38:08.429 --> 00:38:11.429
Yeah, as far as I know.

00:38:11.429 --> 00:38:12.429
She's fine.

00:38:12.429 --> 00:38:21.369
Oliver.

00:38:21.369 --> 00:38:25.260
Happy Turkey Day.

00:38:25.260 --> 00:38:34.239
Where you been? I've been worried about you.

00:38:34.239 --> 00:38:37.289
Yeah.

00:38:37.289 --> 00:38:41.909
Listen, that's all over now.

00:38:41.909 --> 00:38:42.909
I'm like a walking, drug free zone.

00:38:42.909 --> 00:38:43.909
honest.

00:38:43.909 --> 00:38:57.900
So if I were to hug you right now, I wouldn't stab myself on any strain needles.

00:38:57.900 --> 00:39:13.659
I'm so sorry I ever heard you.

00:39:13.659 --> 00:39:27.610
If I could have everyone's attention, please, um, I'd like to make a little announcement.

00:39:27.610 --> 00:39:30.610
Our family has a tradition.

00:39:30.610 --> 00:39:34.610
It goes back way before I was even born.

00:39:34.610 --> 00:39:39.610
Where everyone takes a moment to say what they're most thankful for in their lives.

00:39:39.610 --> 00:39:48.210
I would just like to say that I'm most thankful for

00:39:48.210 --> 00:39:50.210
My mom and dad.

00:39:50.210 --> 00:40:37.530
His faith in me taught me to have faith in myself.

00:40:37.530 --> 00:40:44.269
For me to be love is all it took.

00:40:44.269 --> 00:40:48.269
I'd fall into you if I could, hoping for grace.

00:40:48.269 --> 00:41:20.130
You haven't said a word all night.

00:41:20.130 --> 00:41:23.210
Is everything okay?

00:41:23.210 --> 00:41:25.780
Everything's fine.

00:41:25.780 --> 00:41:34.590
Happy Thanksgiving.

